{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ClosureComponentsSignInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ClosureComponentsSignInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Cycle.Type","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Quotient"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.braidClosureComponents_eq_of_indices_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.braidClosureComponents_eq_of_indices_eq","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L241-L247","doc":"Two braid words differing only in their crossing signs have closures\nwith the same number of components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.braidClosureComponents_resolve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.braidClosureComponents_resolve","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L231-L239","doc":"**The braid-closure statement.** For genuine braid words — the\ncorpus's `BraidWord n = List (Fin (n - 1) × Bool)` — the number of\ncomponents of the closure is unchanged by resolving the crossings any way\nat all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.adjacentPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.adjacentPerm","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L226-L229","doc":"The transposition the crossing at index `i` induces on strands. The\nsign of the crossing is absent by construction, which is the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.strand","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L222-L224","doc":"Strand `i`, as an element of `Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.succStrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.succStrand","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L217-L220","doc":"Strand `i + 1`, as an element of `Fin n`, for a crossing index\n`i : Fin (n - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_ne_of_perm_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_ne_of_perm_ne","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L199-L209","doc":"**The exclusion form.** Distinct component counts force distinct\ninduced permutations.\n\nThis is how the invariant is used in adjudication: a candidate link whose\ncomponent count differs from the word's is excluded, and by\n`closureComponents_resolve` that exclusion survives every choice of\ncrossing sign — so it needs no crossing convention to be fixed first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_eq_of_indices_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_eq_of_indices_eq","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L193-L197","doc":"The same statement for two signed words sharing an index sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_resolve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents_resolve","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L182-L191","doc":"**The component count of a braid closure is a crossing-sign\ninvariant.**\n\nThe count is the same for every resolution of the unsigned word, because\nby `wordPerm_resolve` the permutation it is computed from is the same. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.closureComponents","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L175-L180","doc":"The number of components of the closure of a braid whose induced\npermutation is `π`: the strands `Fin n` fall into components exactly as\nthey fall into orbits of `⟨π⟩`, since the closure joins strand `i` to\nstrand `π i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_resolve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_resolve","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L163-L171","doc":"**Every resolution induces the same permutation.**\n\n`f` and `f'` may disagree at every position; the permutation does not\nmove. This is the statement the deuteron adjudication needs: the mass\nword's `32` resolutions cannot differ in their induced permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolve_indices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolve_indices","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L159-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolveFrom_indices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolveFrom_indices","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L152-L157","doc":"Resolving changes only the signs: the index sequence is preserved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolve","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L148-L150","doc":"Resolve an unsigned word, counting positions from `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolveFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.resolveFrom","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L142-L146","doc":"Resolve an unsigned word, assigning the crossing at position `k` the\nsign `f k`, counting from `k₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_eq_of_indices_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_eq_of_indices_eq","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L120-L133","doc":"**The induced permutation depends only on the crossing indices.**\n\nTwo signed words with the same index sequence induce the same\npermutation, whatever their signs. Every other statement in this file is\na specialisation of this one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_cons","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L116-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm_nil","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L113-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wordPerm","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ClosureComponentsSignInvariant.lean#L104-L111","doc":"The permutation a signed word induces, given an assignment `g` of a\npermutation to each crossing index.\n\nThe `Bool` component of each letter is the crossing's sign, and `g` is not\ngiven it: that omission *is* the mathematical content, since `σᵢ` and\n`σᵢ⁻¹` project to the same transposition in `Sₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}